  "body": "I want to know if it's due to the system or browser version?\n\n- Chrome version： 142.0.7444.162 (arm64)\n- macOS\n\n\n\nThis is an example code：\n\n`\nconst filters = [\n  {\n    vendorId: 0x152A,   // 5418\n    productId: 0x889B,  // 34971\n    usagePage: 0xFF83,  // 65411\n    usage: 0x01\n  }\n];\n\n\n\nasync function getDevice()  {\n  const devices = await navigator.hid.requestDevice({filters});\n  const device = devices[0];\n  console.log(device)\n\n  await device.open();\n\n  device.addEventListener('inputreport', (event) => {\n    const { reportId, data } = event;\n    console.log('Received report', reportId, new Uint8Array(data.buffer));\n  });\n\n \n  const payload = new Uint8Array(63);\n  payload[0] = 0x77; \n  payload[1] = 0x8e; \n  payload[2] = 0x44; \n  payload[3] = 0xac; \n\n\n  try {\n    await device.sendReport(1, payload); // reportId=1\n    console.log('Sent successfully');\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('Send failed:', err);\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div id=\"app\">\n    <button @click=\"getDevice\">getDevice</button>\n  </div>\n</template>\n\n`\n\nAlways displayed “Sent successfully”\n\nbut at chrome://device-log/ However, it will not output any logs",
